@startuml
title OmniDesk Milestone, Sprint, and Release Relationship

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "Product Backlog" as Backlog
rectangle "Sprint Planning" as Planning

package "Milestones" {
  rectangle "M0\nEngineering Foundation" as M0
  rectangle "M1\nAuthentication and Workspace" as M1
  rectangle "M2\nGmail Integration" as M2
  rectangle "M3\nUnified Inbox" as M3
  rectangle "M4\nTelegram Integration" as M4
  rectangle "M5\nProduction Hardening" as M5
}

package "Sprints" {
  rectangle "Sprint 00" as S00
  rectangle "Sprint 01" as S01
  rectangle "Sprint 02" as S02
  rectangle "Sprint 03" as S03
  rectangle "Sprint 04" as S04
  rectangle "Sprint 05" as S05
  rectangle "Sprint 06" as S06
  rectangle "Future Sprint(s)\nAssigned during Sprint Planning" as SF
}

rectangle "Release Review" as Review
rectangle "Versioned Release" as Release

Backlog --> Planning : select items

Planning --> S00 : historical assignment
Planning --> S01 : historical assignment
Planning --> S02 : historical assignment
Planning --> S03 : historical assignment
Planning --> S04 : historical assignment
Planning --> S05 : historical assignment
Planning --> S06 : historical assignment
Planning --> SF : future assignment

S00 --> M0 : primary milestone
S01 --> M0 : primary milestone
S02 --> M1 : primary milestone
S03 --> M1 : primary milestone
S04 --> M2 : primary milestone
S05 --> M2 : primary milestone
S06 --> M3 : primary milestone

SF ..> M4 : allocation TBD
SF ..> M5 : allocation TBD

M0 --> Review : outcome review
M1 --> Review : outcome review
M2 --> Review : outcome review
M3 --> Review : outcome review
M4 --> Review : outcome review
M5 --> Review : outcome review

Review --> Release : release criteria pass

note bottom of SF
Future Sprint numbers are not
reserved in advance.

Sprint numbers and scope are assigned
only during Sprint Planning.
end note

note right of Release
A sprint does not automatically
create a release.

A milestone may contribute to
one or more releases.
end note

@enduml
